<a name="2026-10-06-traditional-wives"> </a>
<h3>Traditional wives</h3>
<p>I lamented in my <a href="blog:2026-10-02">last blog</a> 
that the
 radical left doesn’t like traditional wives. Most women I know want to
 marry a man who she can start a family with, and that includes women
 who have slept with over 100 men. <em>Women want marriage and family,</em>
 so why is the left wing press <a href="AI/2026-10-02-AntiTradWifeNymag.html">publishing articles discouraging  marriage</a>?
<p>Here’s one <a href="AI/2026-10-06-Bower.html">article</a>, 
which
 looks at consent and why we need more than consent to determine whether
 a given sex act is OK; it looks at how a woman is treated overall by
 someone affects how she views sex with them.
<p>There’s a quote <a href="AI/2026-10-06-Bower.html">there</a> 
that
 explains some of the left-wing dislike of traditional marriages:
<blockquote>
<p>a husband who believes, often with the backing of a church that
 teaches wifely submission, that sex is his right and her duty, and who
 treats her like a servant in the rest of their life too. It isn’t the
 commitment that makes the difference. It’s the degree to which he sees
 her as a person or as property.
</blockquote>
<p>Let’s look at what scripture has to say. Let’s go to that part of
 Ephesians which the radical left hates:
<blockquote>
<p>Wives, be submissive to your own husbands, as to the Lord. For the
 husband is the head of the wife, and Christ also is the head of the
 church, being himself the savior of the body. But as the church is
 subject to Christ, so let the wives also be to their own husbands in
 everything.
</blockquote>
<p>Women don’t like being treated as slaves obviously, and Paul who
 wrote this passage agrees. The above scripture continues:
<blockquote>
<p>Husbands, love your wives, even as Christ also loved the church, and
 gave himself up for it; that he might sanctify it, having cleansed it
 by the washing of water with the word, that he might present the church
 to himself gloriously, not having spot or wrinkle or any such thing;
 but that it should be holy and without blemish. Even so husbands also
 ought to love their own wives as their own bodies. He who loves his own
 wife loves himself.
</blockquote>
<p>If men aren’t doing their side of the deal where wives are led by
 their husbands, that is not a marriage following Christian principles.
 Since some men don’t follow both sides of the bargain where the husband
 is in charge, people are understandably turned off by traditional
 marriage.
